Subject: onion-tunnel: ask the per-app DNS limit only for an attributed query, through a function the tests call

The check of the owner (patch 0002) and the check of the per-app limit (patch 0004) were two blocks inside the packet
handler, which no test reaches without a whole tunnel. `admit` is the two together as a function of the owner lookup and
the limit: SERVFAIL when the owner is unknown (the limit is not asked), SERVFAIL when the app is over its limit, the
key otherwise. Behaviour is unchanged. A test pins the address of the DNS listener that the exit app registers as the
DNS server of the Tor network.

--- a/crates/onion-tunnel/src/dns.rs
+++ b/crates/onion-tunnel/src/dns.rs
@@ -629,6 +629,21 @@
         result.map_err(|_| Self::make_answer(query, RCode::ServFail, vec![]))
     }
 
+    /// [`Self::attribute`], then the per-app limit: the SERVFAIL answer too when the app asks faster than `allow` lets it.
+    /// `allow` is asked once, with the key, and not at all for a query whose owner could not be found.
+    fn admit(
+        query: &dns_message_parser::Dns,
+        owner: std::io::Result<u64>,
+        allow: impl FnOnce(u64) -> bool,
+    ) -> Result<u64, dns_message_parser::Dns> {
+        let key = Self::attribute(query, owner)?;
+        if allow(key) {
+            Ok(key)
+        } else {
+            Err(Self::make_answer(query, RCode::ServFail, vec![]))
+        }
+    }
+
